8 #edb/ref 17592186409846 13194139533584 17592186045417 true] [17592186409887 1079 #uuid "d41cebf3-62a2-5784-a1f4-13fc481b665c" 13194139533584 17592186045417 true] [17592186409888 1068 #edb/ref 17592186409886 13194139533584 17592186045417 true] [17592186409888 1069 "q-174385" 13194139533584 17592186045417 true] [17592186409888 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533584 17592186045417 true] [17592186409888 1071 "Given that ${1}_{A}(q)=0,$ which of the following statements about $\\overset{―}{A}$ are true?\n\n- ${1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(q)=1$\n- ${1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(q)=0$\n- $q\\in \\overset{―}{A}$\n\n*Hint: ${1}_{A}$ denotes the indicator function of the set $A$ and ${1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}$ denotes the indicator function of the complement of $A.$*" 13194139533584 17592186045417 true] [17592186409888 1072 #uuid "09ca95e9-e7fd-5d14-80c3-ab64bc50a23d" 13194139533584 17592186045417 true] [17592186409888 1074 "Recall that the indicator functions of $\\overset{―}{A},$ $A\\cap B,$ and $A\\cup B$ have the following properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(x) & =1-{1}_{A}(x) \\\\ {1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(x) & =min{{1}_{A}(x),{1}_{B}(x)} \\\\ {1}_{A\\,\\cup \\,B}\\,(x) & =max{{1}_{A}(x),{1}_{B}(x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true while statement II is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(q) & =1-{1}_{A}(q) \\\\  & =1-0 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since ${1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(q)=1,$ we conclude that $q$ belongs to $\\overset{―}{A}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139533584 17592186045417 true] [17592186409889 1068 #edb/ref 17592186409880 13194139533584 17592186045417 true] [17592186409889 1069 "q-174363" 13194139533584 17592186045417 true] [17592186409889 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533584 17592186045417 true] [17592186409889 1071 "![](images/ae/aeb0c87a33cf30494636f0a8f8d411033ba064385ad04065abff184752ea99d7.png)\n\nWhich of the following is the subset $A$ of $U={-4,-3,-2,-1,0}$ whose indicator function ${1}_{A}(x)$ is shown above?" 13194139533584 17592186045417 true] [17592186409889 1072 #uuid "3574e15c-1d81-5d76-a394-37484fa9dfbb" 13194139533584 17592186045417 true] [17592186409889 1074 "An indicator function maps elements from a set to the values $0$ or $1,$ depending on whether the element belongs to a specified subset. The indicator function is designed to \"indicate\" whether an element is a member of a subset.\n\nMore specifically, consider a universal set $X.$ Then, the indicator function of a set $A⊆X$ is the function\n\n$$\n{1}_{A}(x)={\\begin{aligned}1, & \\text{if }x\\in A, \\\\ 0, & \\text{if }x\\notin A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the diagram above, only the elements $-4$ and $0$ are mapped to $1.$ Therefore, the indicator function in the diagram above corresponds to the set $A={-4,0}.$" 13194139533584 17592186045417 true] [17592186409890 1068 #edb/ref 17592186409881 13194139533584 17592186045417 true] [17592186409890 1069 "q-174402" 13194139533584 17592186045417 true] [17592186409890 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533584 17592186045417 true] [17592186409890 1071 "$$\n{1}_{A}(t)=1,\\,{1}_{B}(t)=1\n$$\n\nGiven the values of the indicator functions of the sets $A$ and $B,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${1}_{A\\,\\cup \\,B}\\,(t)=1$\n- ${1}_{A\\,\\cup \\,B}\\,(t)=0$\n- $t\\in A\\cup B$" 13194139533584 17592186045417 true] [17592186409890 1072 #uuid "6c60efa7-9f70-50c9-8725-0334784ed791" 13194139533584 17592186045417 true] [17592186409890 1074 "Recall that the indicator functions of $\\overset{―}{A},$ $A\\cap B,$ and $A\\cup B$ have the following properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(x) & =1-{1}_{A}(x) \\\\ {1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(x) & =min{{1}_{A}(x),{1}_{B}(x)} \\\\ {1}_{A\\,\\cup \\,B}\\,(x) & =max{{1}_{A}(x),{1}_{B}(x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true while statement II is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}_{A\\,\\cup \\,B}\\,(t) & =max{{1}_{A}(t),{1}_{B}(t)} \\\\  & =max{1,1} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since ${1}_{A\\,\\cup \\,B}\\,(t)=1,$ we conclude that $t$ belongs to $A\\cup B.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139533584 17592186045417 true] [17592186409891 1068 #edb/ref 17592186409883 13194139533584 17592186045417 true] [17592186409891 1069 "q-174394" 13194139533584 17592186045417 true] [17592186409891 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533584 17592186045417 true] [17592186409891 1071 "$$\n{1}_{A}(-1)=1,\\,{1}_{B}(-1)=1\n$$\n\nGiven the values of the indicator functions of the sets $A$ and $B,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(-1)=1$\n- ${1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(-1)=0$\n- $-1\\in A\\cap B$" 13194139533584 17592186045417 true] [17592186409891 1072 #uuid "92b8a61e-f7a9-5e1e-adba-90e2fa6c6243" 13194139533584 17592186045417 true] [17592186409891 1074 "Recall that the indicator functions of $\\overset{―}{A},$ $A\\cap B,$ and $A\\cup B$ have the following properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(x) & =1-{1}_{A}(x) \\\\ {1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(x) & =min{{1}_{A}(x),{1}_{B}(x)} \\\\ {1}_{A\\,\\cup \\,B}\\,(x) & =max{{1}_{A}(x),{1}_{B}(x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true while statement II is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(-1) & =min{{1}_{A}(-1),{1}_{B}(-1)} \\\\  & =min{1,1} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since ${1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(-1)=1,$ we conclude that $-1$ belongs to $A\\cap B.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139533584 17592186045417 true] [17592186409892 1068 #edb/ref 17592186409884 13194139533584 17592186045417 true] [17592186409892 1069 "q-174359" 13194139533584 17592186045417 true] [17592186409892 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533584 17592186045417 true] [17592186409892 1071 "![](images/7c/7c60072882a6effae61da543bfddff1053ab0bcc924d12c49f5acd697b0871c4.png)\n\nWhich of the following is the subset $A$ of $U={a,b,c,d,e}$ whose indicator function ${1}_{A}(x)$ is shown above?" 13194139533584 17592186045417 true] [17592186409892 1072 #uuid "a66f5e5d-805e-5011-9534-19a9e92d3193" 13194139533584 17592186045417 true] [17592186409892 1074 "An indicator function maps elements from a set to the values $0$ or $1,$ depending on whether the element belongs to a specified subset. The indicator function is designed to \"indicate\" whether an element is a member of a subset.\n\nMore specifically, consider a universal set $X.$ Then, the indicator function of a set $A⊆X$ is the function\n\n$$\n{1}_{A}(x)={\\begin{aligned}1, & \\text{if }x\\in A, \\\\ 0, & \\text{if }x\\notin A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the diagram above, only the elements $b,c$ and $e$ are mapped to $1.$ Therefore, the indicator function in the diagram above corresponds to the set $A={b,c,e}.$" 13194139533584 17592186045417 true] [17592186409893 1068 #edb/ref 17592186409885 13194139533584 17592186045417 true] [17592186409893 1069 "q-174380" 13194139533584 17592186045417 true] [17592186409893 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533584 17592186045417 true] [17592186409893 1071 "Given that ${1}_{A}(0)=0,$ which of the following statements about $\\overset{―}{A}$ are true?\n\n- ${1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(0)=1$\n- ${1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(0)=0$\n- $0\\in \\overset{―}{A}$\n\n*Hint: ${1}_{A}$ denotes the indicator function of the set $A$ and ${1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}$ denotes the indicator function of the complement of $A.$*" 13194139533584 17592186045417 true] [17592186409893 1072 #uuid "a8a05322-998a-5d01-8b89-68a8bc93dd0f" 13194139533584 17592186045417 true] [17592186409893 1074 "Recall that the indicator functions of $\\overset{―}{A},$ $A\\cap B,$ and $A\\cup B$ have the following properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(x) & =1-{1}_{A}(x) \\\\ {1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(x) & =min{{1}_{A}(x),{1}_{B}(x)} \\\\ {1}_{A\\,\\cup \\,B}\\,(x) & =max{{1}_{A}(x),{1}_{B}(x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true while statement II is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(0) & =1-{1}_{A}(0) \\\\  & =1-0 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since ${1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(0)=1,$ we conclude that $0$ belongs to $\\overset{―}{A}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139533584 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-06dd1182-e612-5525-b9de-c12d2d05c3e6" 17592186409840 "answer-1325aba8-981f-532b-b892-12eb6305d32e" 17592186409841 "answer-14622146-9357-5002-bb58-2d5df436755d" 17592186409842 "answer-1682b7b8-dbb8-5c5c-8816-d4c1a452d7d3" 17592186409843 "answer-1737c9b3-9afe-57ff-999b-4fa97a61723d" 17592186409844 "answer-1a0cc322-449d-5a1c-a8d7-1039e1ba0529" 17592186409845 "answer-2fd26958-8f1d-57a3-abb9-807967b6f0e5" 17592186409846 "answer-315c03d9-5543-5355-95b3-ced1d45e7088" 17592186409847 "answer-31e4f699-7440-595b-9f7d-fd1e34e533f9" 17592186409848 "answer-357a177c-678c-5efe-b182-20eab09b9991" 17592186409849 "answer-3df49fbd-f52c-571e-843c-9a57fe7a2605" 17592186409850 "answer-3e0876cb-849b-532e-9b46-8b0f0fdbeb1e" 17592186409851 "answer-4068f7e2-a0ab-5191-84b6-5c4067339274" 17592186409852 "answer-43e6f09d-b15b-583f-b322-ed2cb2110fd7" 17592186409853 "answer-49cb469a-be52-5791-8807-8b802f15d5ed" 17592186409854 "answer-4dbbb73e-91a8-55fd-a1de-9d7b3f028b3c" 17592186409855 "answer-618b2a8e-572b-5ad5-b3c0-c1a42f8e3e99" 17592186409856 "answer-6b58a9c1-6929-5a77-a9db-024a96962cb7" 17592186409857 "answer-6e77902f-8af5-5f32-b8fb-71bb215e7d20" 17592186409858 "answer-6ee506d6-f345-54fa-9845-d354cdc4d92e" 17592186409859 "answer-7bdeb40f-7a93-51cd-bc84-fa02eb15dc72" 17592186409860 "answer-844ca5b4-a0c6-5ba0-9623-57c490152861" 17592186409861 "answer-9366fcca-3b9b-567c-9045